19:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"The exam provides a formula sheet, so memorizing area and volume formulas is not where your study time belongs. Knowing the sheet exists and being able to find the right formula on it quickly is worth more. Print it out and practice with it, so it is familiar rather than a new document on test day."]}]
1a:["$","$L1e","5",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A jacket costs $60 and is marked 25% off. What is the sale price?","options":["$$35","$$45","$$48","$$15"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"25% of 60 is 15, so the discount is $15 and the price is $45. The faster route is to multiply by what you pay rather than what you save: 60 × 0.75 = 45, one operation instead of two.","optionRationales":["$$35 would be a discount of $25, which is about 42%.","Correct. $60 − $15 = $45, or 60 × 0.75 in one step.","$$48 would be a 20% discount.","$$15 is the discount, not the sale price — a very common misread of the question."]}}]
